{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FCnGC27BBSC5RKcnozMUmj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd064-shuf\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/shuf: Shuffle Lines Randomly\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts and data pipelines use shuf to randomly permute input lines, select random\n6\t  samples, or generate random numbers within a range. The macOS BSD system has no built-in\n7\t  shuf command. GNU shuf from coreutils supports input from files or stdin, range generation,\n8\t  head count limiting, and repeat mode. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n9\t  reference binary (gshuf, installed by coreutils) in output format and exit codes, verified\n10\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils. Because shuf output is non-deterministic,\n11\t  differential tests verify structural properties (line count, value ranges, uniqueness)\n12\t  rather than exact byte equality.\n13\t\n14\tgoals:\n15\t  - G1: Randomly permute input lines from files or stdin.\n16\t  - G2: Support integer range generation via -i LO-HI.\n17\t  - G3: Support output count limiting via -n COUNT and repeat mode via -r.\n18\t\n19\trequirements:\n20\t  R1:\n21\t    title: Default shuffle behavior\n22\t    items:\n23\t      - R1.1:\n24\t          text: When given one or more FILE arguments, must read all lines from each file, randomly permute them, and write the result to stdout.\n25\t      - R1.2:\n26\t          text: When no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is given as a filename, must read from stdin.\n27\t      - R1.3:\n28\t          text: Must output each input line exactly once in a random order (a permutation, not sampling with replacement) unless -r is given.\n29\t      - R1.4:\n30\t          text: Must treat each line as terminated by a newline. The last line need not end with a newline, but must be included in the shuffle.\n31\t\n32\t  R2:\n33\t    title: Range mode and output control\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R2.1:\n36\t          text: \"-i LO-HI or --input-range=LO-HI must generate and shuffle integers from LO to HI inclusive, one per line. Must not be combined with file arguments.\"\n37\t      - R2.2:\n38\t          text: \"-n COUNT or --head-count=COUNT must output at most COUNT lines.\"\n39\t      - R2.3:\n40\t          text: \"-r or --repeat must allow output lines to repeat (sampling with replacement). Without -n, runs indefinitely.\"\n41\t      - R2.4:\n42\t          text: \"-o FILE or --output=FILE must write output to FILE instead of stdout.\"\n43\t\n44\t  R3:\n45\t    title: Random source and zero-delimiter\n46\t    items:\n47\t      - R3.1:\n48\t          text: \"--random-source=FILE must read random bytes from FILE instead of the system random source.\"\n49\t      - R3.2:\n50\t          text: \"-z or --zero-terminated must use NUL (\\\\0) as the line delimiter instead of newline, for both input and output.\"\n51\t      - R3.3:\n52\t          text: \"-e or --echo must treat each ARG as an input line instead of reading from files.\"\n53\t      - R3.4:\n54\t          text: Must handle empty input (zero lines) by producing no output and exiting 0.\n55\t\n56\t  R4:\n57\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n58\t    items:\n59\t      - R4.1:\n60\t          text: Must exit 0 on successful operation.\n61\t      - R4.2:\n62\t          text: Must exit 1 on error (invalid range, conflicting options, write error).\n63\t      - R4.3:\n64\t          text: \"Differential tests must verify structural properties rather than exact output: correct line count, values within range for -i, no duplicates without -r, duplicates allowed with -r.\"\n65\t      - R4.4:\n66\t          text: \"Tests must cover: shuffle stdin lines, shuffle file lines, -i range mode, -n head count, -r repeat mode, -e echo mode, -z zero-terminated, empty input, and error cases (invalid range, -i with files).\"\n67\t\n68\tnon_goals:\n69\t  - cmd/shuf does not guarantee a specific PRNG algorithm or reproducible output for a given random seed.\n70\t  - cmd/shuf does not implement --random-source with /dev/urandom compatibility testing (the random source changes output).\n71\t\n72\tacceptance_criteria:\n73\t  - id: AC1\n74\t    criterion: \"printf 'a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/shuf produces exactly 3 lines containing a, b, c in some order.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.1\n77\t      - R1.2\n78\t      - R1.3\n79\t      - R1.4\n80\t  - id: AC2\n81\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/shuf -i 1-5 -n 3 produces exactly 3 distinct integers from 1 to 5.\"\n82\t    traces:\n83\t      - R2.1\n84\t      - R2.2\n85\t  - id: AC3\n86\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/shuf -e alpha beta gamma produces exactly 3 lines containing alpha, beta, gamma in some order.\"\n87\t    traces:\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t      - R4.1\n90\t  - id: AC4\n91\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/shuf -i 1-5 -r -n 10 produces exactly 10 integers each between 1 and 5 (duplicates allowed).\"\n92\t    traces:\n93\t      - R2.1\n94\t      - R2.2\n95\t      - R2.3\n96\t  - id: AC5\n97\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gshuf passes for all structural checks listed in R4.4.\"\n98\t    traces:\n99\t      - R4.3\n100\t      - R4.4\n101\t  - id: AC6\n102\t    criterion: \"cmd/shuf compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n103\t    traces:\n104\t      - R1.1\n105\t      - R1.2\n106\t      - R1.3\n107\t      - R1.4\n108\t      - R2.1\n109\t      - R2.2\n110\t      - R2.3\n111\t      - R2.4\n112\t      - R3.1\n113\t      - R3.2\n114\t      - R3.3\n115\t      - R3.4\n116\t      - R4.1\n117\t      - R4.2\n118\t      - R4.3\n119\t      - R4.4\n120\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47895cbe-856d-4389-8852-374f7a40f991","uuid":"994909c4-4766-4c56-8bd1-51fc234ae145","timestamp":"2026-05-21T17:52:51.671Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5429/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd064-shuf.yaml","content":"id: srd064-shuf\ntitle: \"cmd/shuf: Shuffle Lines Randomly\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts and data pipelines use shuf to randomly permute input lines, select random\n  samples, or generate random numbers within a range. The macOS BSD system has no built-in\n  shuf command. GNU shuf from coreutils supports input from files or stdin, range generation,\n  head count limiting, and repeat mode. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (gshuf, installed by coreutils) in output format and exit codes, verified\n  by differential testing via pkg/testutils. Because shuf output is non-deterministic,\n  differential tests verify structural properties (line count, value ranges, uniqueness)\n  rather than exact byte equality.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Randomly permute input lines from files or stdin.\n  - G2: Support integer range generation via -i LO-HI.\n  - G3: Support output count limiting via -n COUNT and repeat mode via -r.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default shuffle behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When given one or more FILE arguments, must read all lines from each file, randomly permute them, and write the result to stdout.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is given as a filename, must read from stdin.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must output each input line exactly once in a random order (a permutation, not sampling with replacement) unless -r is given.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must treat each line as terminated by a newline. The last line need not end with a newline, but must be included in the shuffle.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Range mode and output control\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-i LO-HI or --input-range=LO-HI must generate and shuffle integers from LO to HI inclusive, one per line. Must not be combined with file arguments.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-n COUNT or --head-count=COUNT must output at most COUNT lines.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-r or --repeat must allow output lines to repeat (sampling with replacement). Without -n, runs indefinitely.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-o FILE or --output=FILE must write output to FILE instead of stdout.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Random source and zero-delimiter\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"--random-source=FILE must read random bytes from FILE instead of the system random source.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-z or --zero-terminated must use NUL (\\\\0) as the line delimiter instead of newline, for both input and output.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"-e or --echo must treat each ARG as an input line instead of reading from files.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: Must handle empty input (zero lines) by producing no output and exiting 0.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on successful operation.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on error (invalid range, conflicting options, write error).\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Differential tests must verify structural properties rather than exact output: correct line count, values within range for -i, no duplicates without -r, duplicates allowed with -r.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: shuffle stdin lines, shuffle file lines, -i range mode, -n head count, -r repeat mode, -e echo mode, -z zero-terminated, empty input, and error cases (invalid range, -i with files).\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/shuf does not guarantee a specific PRNG algorithm or reproducible output for a given random seed.\n  - cmd/shuf does not implement --random-source with /dev/urandom compatibility testing (the random source changes output).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"printf 'a\\\\nb\\\\nc\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/shuf produces exactly 3 lines containing a, b, c in some order.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/shuf -i 1-5 -n 3 produces exactly 3 distinct integers from 1 to 5.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/shuf -e alpha beta gamma produces exactly 3 lines containing alpha, beta, gamma in some order.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/shuf -i 1-5 -r -n 10 produces exactly 10 integers each between 1 and 5 (duplicates allowed).\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gshuf passes for all structural checks listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/shuf compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":120,"startLine":1,"totalLines":120}}}
